0..76 Comment "// Structural equality derived from a declaration\'s levitated code (Chapman,"
77..150 Comment "// Dagand, McBride and Morris, _The Gentle Art of Levitation_, ICFP 2010,"
151..228 Comment "// doi:10.1145/1863543.1863547). `Nat`\'s code is `1` for `Zero` and `var Nat`"
229..305 Comment "// for `Succ`; `Tagged`\'s is one product of two fields, a builtin `Bool` and"
306..386 Comment "// `Nat`. `Eq.generic(T)` reads that code — the constructor table, the product"
387..465 Comment "// spine, a `var` as the recursion and each leaf at the type it names — into"
466..538 Comment "// closed core the checker judges as written and the kernel replays; the"
539..616 Comment "// derivation itself is never trusted. A family whose code takes a parameter,"
617..655 Comment "// or a mutual pair, is refused beside"
656..720 Comment "// `../../pathological/metaprograms/derive-eq-over-codes.gandr`."
722..776 Comment "/// Unary naturals: a unit and a recursive occurrence."
